      "problem": "$\\frac{5}{2}q-\\frac{7}{6}q=${{field-1}}\n$q$",
      "worked_solution": "We combine the like terms by subtracting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}q-\\frac{7}{6}q & = \\\\ (\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{6})q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to subtract the coefficients, we have to convert them to have the same denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{6})q & = \\\\ (\\frac{15}{6}-\\frac{7}{6})q & = \\\\ (\\frac{15-7}{6})q & = \\\\ \\frac{8}{6}q & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$",
